  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0049 database is a comprehensive system for managing various entities and their relationships. At its core, it contains information about businesses, which are categorized and can be associated with domains and owners. Each business has its own set of services, which are categorized into types and can be offered by human resources, who are also associated with businesses and contacts. The appointments table stores information about scheduled appointments, which can be linked to various entities such as contacts, businesses, services, human resources, and vacancies. The vacancies table stores information about available time slots for services, which can be linked to businesses, services, and human resources. The notifications system allows for categorization and grouping of notifications, which can be sent to users based on their roles and preferences. The users table stores information about registered users, including their roles and permissions, which are managed through the roles and permissions tables. The preferences table stores user-specific settings, and the password resets table stores information about password reset requests. The countries table stores information about countries, and the categories table stores information about categories for businesses and services. The migrations table stores information about database migrations, and the notification categories and groups tables store information about notification categories and groups. The role-user and permission-user tables store information about user roles and permissions, and the role-permission table stores information about role-permission relationships. The service types table stores information about service types, and the services table stores information about individual services offered by businesses.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context:\n\nThe project involves developing an online appointments platform named Timegrid. It is designed to facilitate scheduling and reservation of booking slots, adaptable to diverse industries. It enables seamless coordination between contractors and customers to find the ideal meeting times through online appointments.\n\n2) Objectives:\n\n- Provide a flexible platform for scheduling and booking appointments across various industries.\n- Enhance business management through a comprehensive interface for handling services, clients, staff, and availability.\n- Provide secure authentication and user management features.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users:\n\n- Contractors/Businesses: Utilize the platform to manage appointments, services, and staff availability.\n- Customers: Book appointments and interact with businesses via the platform.\n- Administrators: Oversee platform operations and ensure system integrity.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions:\n\n- User Authentication: Supports traditional and OAuth2 sign-in/sign-up using Socialite.\n- Business Management: Includes tools for managing business details, client address books, services, and staff.\n- Appointment Scheduling: Users can schedule appointments using a date picker and view schedules through fullcalendar.\n- Calendar Integration: Share calendars via iCalendar links.\n- Notifications: Basic email notifications are available for appointment reminders and updates.\n- Internationalization (i18n): Support for multiple languages.\n- Timezone Management: Handles multiple timezones to cater to a global user base.\n- Communication: Facilitates live chat through TidioChat.\n- Admin Interface: Features an administration GUI built with AdminLTE and Twitter Bootstrap 3 theme.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions:\n\n- Scalability: Designed to handle a significant number of appointments and users.\n- Security: Secure authentication processes and data management.\n- Usability: Intuitive interfaces for both desktop and mobile access.\n- Reliability: Ensures consistent performance and uptime for users globally.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0049.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0049\nCREATE TABLE `businesses` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `businesses_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `categories` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `businesses_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `categories` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `contacts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `contacts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `human_resources` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `human_resources_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `services` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `service_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `services_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `services_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`service_type_id`) REFERENCES `service_types` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `service_types` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `appointments` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `contact_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `business_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `human_resource_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `appointment_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`contact_id`) REFERENCES `contacts` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`business_id`) REFERENCES `businesses` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `services` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `appointments_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`human_resource_id`) REFERENCES `human_resources` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vacancies` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `service_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `human_resource_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `available_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `vacancies_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`service_id`) REFERENCES `services` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `vacancies_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`human_resource_id`) REFERENCES `human_resources` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `users` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `users_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `roles` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permissions` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role_user` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`, `user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `roles` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `role_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permission_user` (\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`permission_id`, `user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `permission_user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`permission_id`) REFERENCES `permissions` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `permission_user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `preferences` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `settings` json NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `preferences_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `password_resets` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reset_token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `password_resets_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `countries` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notifications` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `notification_category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notifications_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `users` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `notifications_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`notification_category_id`) REFERENCES `notification_categories` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notification_categories` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notification_groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `migrations` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `migration` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `batch` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
